Step 5 of the plan to make the `--call` door work for an agent that cannot use MCP (Anthony, 2026-10-01; his ideas 1, 7, 8 and 11 in using_call.md).

Today the route rests on one user's hand-written VS Code instructions file, which init and update neither install nor refresh. Calls are recorded as `reflow2-mcp --call`, and nothing tests the route.

MUST:
- `reflow2 init --harness vscode` (or its own harness name) writes `.github/instructions/reflow2.instructions.md` from text the BINARY serves, so `reflow2 update` refreshes it. The starting text is Anthony's working file.
- Skill stubs go in `.github/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`: frontmatter plus one line saying to fetch the skill with get_skill. The body stays served (req:thin-install).
- Door calls can be attributed to the product that made them, so usage_report tells VS Code from a Makefile.
- A CI test drives the binary the way the instructions tell an agent to:
  - discovery;
  - an exit-2 refusal naming the missing argument;
  - a write on a free graph;
  - a refused write and a snapshot read on a held graph;
  - an export.
  This keeps served text that says "call X" true through the door (dec:one-reflow2-serves-both-routes-mcp-and-the-call-door).
